From 9b4066e55c458d63358448de117dfb24482212e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 04:05:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PUBLISH-FIX-109: ghost candidates - the top refusal in the
 app was no book

Owner directive: "No blocks. Trace that line from end to end."

Live, eb532bba, one 15-minute window after the stage widened to twenty:

  JUDGE FUNNEL: 19 candidates; crossings 201 -> confirmations 64
                -> decisions 48, entries 0
  top refusals: FEED_NOT_IN_TAPE_UNIVERSE 36, FI15 22,
                PRIOR_MID_RESPONSE_SMALL 19, RV60 18, ...

The most common refusal in the whole application was not a gate. The
volatility watch ranks ~90 movers; the deep tape has 20 slots. The
Judge was offered the whole ranked list, admitted coins with no order
book, burned a preparation slot on each, and refused them for the only
reason it could - there was nothing to look at. Nineteen candidates
where twenty were prepared: seats held by ghosts while runners with
live books waited.

The tape's current-universe record is the truth about what has a book
(tape/run.js re-merges the carried hot pairs after every selection), so
the extra sources are filtered against it. Nothing judgeable is
dropped: a mover with no book is not a missed opportunity, it is a
nomination the Judge cannot act on. An empty or unreadable record falls
back to the old unfiltered list, so a boot never nominates nothing.
Adoption is untouched - the hot lane reads the watch picks itself every
15 s (FIX-102), never through this path - so a runner gets its book on
the next adoption pass and the Judge on the pass after, with a free
slot waiting. What is withheld is counted and printed: OFF-TAPE: n.

Also: the second look showed `flow-only refusals 20 -> armed 0,
dropped 0` and the missing word was `superseded` - a natural re-crossing
beat the retake to it, which is the BETTER outcome and was uncounted in
the line. The counter always existed; now it is printed.

Fenced by test/publish-fix-109-no-ghost-candidates.test.js (6).

